# Grayscale UI

Ledger is a calm, minimal practice log. All UI must be **grayscale only**.

## Allowed palette

Use Tailwind `zinc` (and neutral structural tokens like `white`, `black`, `transparent`):

- Backgrounds: `bg-zinc-50`, `bg-white`, `bg-zinc-100`
- Text: `text-zinc-900`, `text-zinc-800`, `text-zinc-700`, `text-zinc-600`, `text-zinc-500`, `text-zinc-400`
- Borders: `border-zinc-200`, `border-zinc-300`
- Interactive / emphasis: `bg-zinc-900`, `hover:bg-zinc-800`, `ring-zinc-900`

## Do not use

No semantic or accent color scales in templates or inline JS class strings:

- `red`, `green`, `emerald`, `blue`, `amber`, `yellow`, `orange`, `purple`, `pink`, `indigo`, `cyan`, `teal`, `rose`, `violet`, `lime`, `sky`, `fuchsia`

This includes flash messages, outcome panels, linked-entry callouts, required-field markers, and delete/remove buttons.

## Examples

```html
<!-- BAD -->
<div class="border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-900">...</div>
<span class="text-red-600">*</span>

<!-- GOOD -->
<div class="border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-900">...</div>
<span class="text-zinc-500">*</span>
```

Use weight, border, and background contrast — not hue — to distinguish sections.
